> >That has to be malglico!
> 
> And malrusko and malspano, from the sound of it

The same word also denotes {nu citka} and {se citka} in Hindi
(where one even says <khAnA khAnA> `eat eating --> a meal' for
`dine'), Chinese and, I'm sure, Arabic.  I can't claim that
this metonymy is common to all natlangs, but it is certainly
very common.  Which doesn't make it acceptable in Lojban, though.

